<title>USA: Four Corners NM power plant restart delayed a day.</title>
<headline>Four Corners NM power plant restart delayed a day.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Restart of the 755 megawatt (MW) unit 4 at the Four Corners coal-fired generating station in New Mexico was pushed back one day to Thursday after it was tentatively scheduled to start up today, the operator said.</p>
<p>&quot;It ought to be up tomorrow,&quot; said a spokesman for Arizona Public Service Co, adding more time was needed for repairs.</p>
<p>Four Corners unit 4 was shut when a booster fan failed.</p>
<p>Arizona Public Service, a subsidiary of Pinnacle West Capital Corp, holds a 15 percent interest in the unit.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622))</p>
